f large-scale data centers. The pause, which will last up to a year, is the nationâ€™s first statewide ban on data centers, which have drawn increasing concern from lawmakers and citizens based on their impact on electricity prices and the energy grid. â€œAs data center development threatens to hike up utility bills, deplete our natural resources, and create uncertainty for New Yorkers, itâ€™s my responsibility to take action and lead,â€ Hochul said in a&nbsp; statement . Technology companies have invested billions of dollars to build data centers all across the country, driven in part by the computing demands from artificial intelligence. In her executive order, Hochul directed the state Department of Public Service to issue no new permits for large-scale data centers for a&nbsp; year. During that period, the agency will conduct an environmental analysis on the impacts of data centers, along with a proceeding to â€œrequire data centers to either pay more for their energy or supply their own.â€ New York lawmakers passed a more extensive&nbsp; data center moratorium &nbsp;last month, but Hochul has not said whether she will sign the bill. Read Next Climate activists take on a new foe: Data centers Kate Yoder Maine Governor Janet Mills, also a Democrat, vetoed a measure earlier this year that would have been the first statewide data center ban. In a news release, Hochul also directed the stateâ€™s economic development agency to develop a framework that local communities can use to negotiate with tech companies that seek to construct data centers. That framework will focus on infrastructure improvements, child care investments, direct financial support, and labor and wage standards. She also announced plans for a fund that would require data centers to invest in New Yorkâ€™s grid infrastructure and clean energy supply. And she called on lawmakers to repeal the stateâ€™s sales tax exemptions for large data centers. Across the country, data centers have drawn vocal opposition at local public meetings and in state capitols. Several cities and counties will vote on ballot measures this year to restrict the development of new data centers. This story was originally published by Grist with the headline New York governor orders first statewide data center moratorium on Jul 18, 2026.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ImaAtKqtYrg21NLWOLO-3SuJgbmL9QC0iAJSnSKlOtMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx?New York governor orders first statewide data center moratoriumƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;uzZOkmOc6wJROjMYuKDJGRz0TRk1USCPp1-h02MdE7Iƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkoSyndicationItemƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Z73KrbrA9dGk3258-_OKy5qpEYSdgTauDb7uRMygdkgƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx[https://grist.org/politics/new-york-governor-orders-first-statewide-data-center-moratorium/ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;gRO0-f3rHW26kUvEAzGyYGWQ9zJd-g5vZPlx13xOw60ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx?new-york-governor-orders-first-statewide-data-center-moratoriumƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;l2_XlAPeT1ti2iFndxg6NyA1-Iqnrd4FEaDdx9CNd88ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwSyndicationSourceBundleƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;FCidE9hU0zNaX8EKNUNzBc4a3B8F6xhIJ7FNOx00K6Mƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkkenvironmentƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;j_HlVcao7Z4FseKlV1sN2FHFpNsjrqu262Zt2lOFW0wƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;kIsvzd4zXzrUTCQl6CvzOy